{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>For the threshing sledge.</b> It is like the instrument with which one crushes, like חָרוּץ חָדָשׁ (Isaiah 41:15):" "<b>For the cummin he does not turn.</b> For the meaning is: he does not drag [it] after its people:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "Rendered חרוץ as 'threshing sledge' following the verse context; Ibn Ezra's comparison is to a crushing tool."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:42.782872835Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}